A.append(dict(next(a for a in A if a['id'] == 'oozing-horror' and a['pack'] == 4), pack=11))

# Pack 12: ogric-abomination call 1 (pack 5) failed the base_drift gate (-10.64, tolerance +-8) and warned subject_intrusion: the raised maul and the big stone arm pushed out toward the rim and the plate around the heavy figure came out darker. Second call for this asset: same ogre, drawn smaller with the maul shortened and held close, the disc held at reference lightness.
OA_FIT = " Calibration from the previous generation of this exact token: the design (hulking grey-mauve ogre, one huge pale stone golem arm with violet-cyan runes, bolted stone plates, raised greatmaul) was right and readable, but the maul and the stone arm pushed out toward the disc rim and the plate came out darker than the reference. This time keep the same ogre, but draw it clearly SMALLER, everything inside a circle of about 0.55 of the disc radius, centred, with the greatmaul a SHORT-handled maul held diagonally close beside the head (its head no higher than the top of the head and no farther out than the shoulder) and the stone arm bent with the boulder fist held close in front of the chest; render the WHOLE disc, its outer ring band and the plate under and around the figure, at exactly the style reference lightness or a hair lighter, evenly all round, with no cast shadow, contact shadow or darkening beside the figure."
_oa = next(a for a in A if a['id'] == 'ogric-abomination')
retry('ogric-abomination', 12, comp=COMP + FIT + COMPACT + BRIGHT + DARKFIX + CATS + TIGHT + OA_FIT,
      subject=_oa['subject'].replace('a big brown wooden GREATMAUL raised diagonally over the shoulder', 'a SHORT-handled brown wooden GREATMAUL held diagonally close beside the head').replace('ending in a boulder fist with glowing VIOLET-CYAN RUNES', 'bent with the boulder fist held close in front of the chest, glowing with VIOLET-CYAN RUNES'))

# Pack 13 (48px floor review, before shipping): vampire-lord pack-8 export passes every numeric gate (masked luminance 70.4, drift -2.66, radius 0.8585) but is the weakest figure on the real floors: small, and a dull mustard-brown mass with little value contrast. Third and last call for this asset. Same noble, brightened and drawn a little larger.
VL_READ = " READABILITY REFINEMENT (the previous generation of this exact token passed the numeric gates but read as a small dull mustard-brown mass at 48 pixels): keep the same noble, but lift every value and fill the disc better: a BRIGHT saffron-yellow and cream-gold long tunic with large near-white highlight planes and a broad bright gold sash, a bright pale face, a heavy cloak in warm light bronze-tan whose lining is a big bright vivid CRIMSON-RED panel clearly visible behind the shoulders, light tan boots, a bright silver-white rapier with a broad white edge highlight, and only the hair and eye slits dark; the figure fills the inner three quarters of the disc (a circle of about 0.68 of the disc radius, centred) as a bright shape on the dark plate, the rapier short and held close, the cloak hanging close behind; no dark brown or black cloth anywhere; render the whole disc and its plate at exactly the style reference lightness, with no cast shadow."
_vl2 = next(a for a in A if a['id'] == 'vampire-lord' and a['pack'] == 8)
retry('vampire-lord', 13, comp=COMP + FIT + COMPACT + BRIGHT + DARKFIX + VL_FIT + VL_READ, subject=_vl2['subject'])
